  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 254 AM EST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\n- Dry and warmer through Wednesday\n\nLatest IR loop shows most of the Lower Peninsula covered in a\nstratocu deck; 00Z raobs reveal a stout inversion around h85 that\nis trapping moisture underneath. Across the UP and southern\nCanada, drier air was working south skies were clearing. As the\nupper low to the east moves away, high pressure over the MS Valley\nwill move over the Great Lakes and we'll see decreasing clouds\nthis afternoon.\n\nTemperatures will be on the upswing this week due to increasing\nheights aloft. H8 temperatures near -4c this morning will rise to\n+8 by Thursday. This will result in highs climbing from the mid\n40s today to upper 50s by Thursday. \n\n- Chance of rain Thursday/Saturday, Mild\n\nThe next chance (around 30 percent) of rain arrives Thursday as a\nweak cold front moves through. There's virtually no cold air\nbehind this front and the low associated with it is north of Lake\nSuperior. Thus, that 30 PoP over the northwest CWA Thursday may be\ngenerous. \n\nThe larger focus comes over the weekend, when a high amplitude\ntrough over the West Coast move east. That wave is progd to phase\nwith a short wave dropping south from Canada and producing a\ndeeper low over the upper MS Valley. The cold front associated\nwith that low will then move east late Saturday. That means a very\nmild day Saturday...highs in the lower 60s, before showers move\nthrough ahead of the front.",
